# RANCHO core

Before meaningful RANCHO work:

1. Read [docs/START-HERE.md](../../docs/START-HERE.md).
2. Load only the authoritative context for this task. How to choose it is in [docs/ai/context-guide.md](../../docs/ai/context-guide.md).
3. Respect [docs/product/constitution.md](../../docs/product/constitution.md).
4. Respect the accepted domain and architecture sources named in Start Here.
5. Keep changes within the approved scope.
6. Do not promote a future possibility into a current requirement.
7. Do not silently redefine a ranch fact or product policy.
8. An important accepted decision must be recorded in the repository.
9. If a conflict exists, surface it before proceeding.
10. Apply [docs/product/uncertainty-protocol.md](../../docs/product/uncertainty-protocol.md).

Hold these together: profitability and sustainable ranch value; realistic UX and adoption; reliable reusable data and responsible evolution.

A review stays read-only unless the user explicitly asks for edits. Humans retain the authority defined in the Constitution.

This rule does not replace those documents. No production application is scaffolded. Do not assume `apps/api` or `apps/web` exists.
